n they did back in 2014 so a complete  route of the opposite position by the  ruling BJP  so Modi had as we said a decisive  Victory but he's got a lot of challenges  facing him for his next term what do you  think is going to be top of his agenda  well I'm afraid there are actually no  challenges to the Prime Minister  Narendra Modi government I did mention  Pharma distress I did mention higher  unemployment the the economy has been  floundering in different ways but none  of this seems to matter because the  Mandate that he has been awarded seems  to say that the last five years have  actually been great let's get more of  that so while of course these are issues  a government has to address he has  talked about leading an inclusive  government leading a government that  that rises above cost politics and  religion politics it we will have to  wait and watch what exactly this  government chooses to focus on will they  address the issues that have been raised  when they are being criticized or will  they just take this mandate to plow on  ahead with just about a free hand in  whatever they wish to do they have  almost a two-thirds majority in in  Parliament including their Coalition so  of course a very strong hand and we'll  just have to wait and watch exactly how  they select how they choose to exercise  this Faith this trust mandate that they  have been awarded DW correspondent  nimisha jaiswal in Delhi for us thank  you so much
 

